    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0365" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg365"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 23, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of August 28, No. 14, has
                    been received. We await with some interest the explanations of the government of
                    the Netherlands concerning the affair at Curaçoa, but at the same time with very
                    great confidence that it will be conformable to the good and friendly relations
                    existing between the two countries.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S. Pike</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c..</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
